{
  "case_id": "2021-21-12",
  "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Federal Election Commission",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Appellees' suit should be dismissed for lack of standing, but if the Court reaches the merits, it should reverse the district court's judgment and hold that the statutory loan repayment limit is constitutional."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Stewart, other than Section 304, is there any other basis for enforcing the regulation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Yeah, the coffee sounds like -- what's the tort doctrine that used to be, you know, two workers and you say it's his fault, and the other one says, well, you did a lot of this yourself?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: I mean, there's contributory negligence --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I did allude earlier to TransUnion. And, in TransUnion, the Court said, if a plaintiff has not suffered concrete harm as a result of the defendant's legal violation, then the suit can't go forward, even if Congress has created an express cause of action with a statutory damages remedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Why isn't the 2900 limit that applies sufficient to address the anti- -- government's anti-corruption interest, especially given, as Justice Barrett says, it is a loan, not a gift?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Stewart, just a couple of questions to satisfy my curiosity. One on the merits. Could you --if you determine -- if the government determined that certain media outlets had an outsized influence on election, could it similarly limit the amount that they spend on editorials to equalize the influence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: I don't quite see the difference, but, okay. My final question is, going back to your standing, you -- you said a number of times that these self-inflicted injuries can't be a basis for standing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I -- I'm not sure I understand your explanation why the repayment of this loan is a gift when the repayment of other loans is never considered a gift."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I'm curious. In that case, you have the intervention by a third party. You don't have the repayment of the loan by the person who -- to whom the loan was given in the first place."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counselor, the Chief asked a question about how do you determine where the risk of corruption arises. Congress has chosen the $250,000 figure. But I guess what he was asking is, is that figure defensible and on the basis of what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Charles J. Cooper (appellees)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government's arguments against Senator Cruz's standing are meritless."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Cooper, could you just take a minute and tell us exactly whose -- how this loan repayment regulation or provision affects speech or impedes speech? Is it the speech of candidate -- of Senator Cruz? Is it the speech of his donors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Charles J. Cooper (appellees)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It most dominantly burdens and creates a drag on the campaign's speech, on the candidate's speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So -- so this restriction, which is a restriction on loan repayment, is really a restriction on how a candidate can use third parties to finance his speech, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cooper",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't know what\nconstitutional challenge I would have to the\nregulation, other than the notion that it was\narbitrary and capricious. And, yes, we did\nmake that claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Surely, Your Honor, the\n-- the injury, the actual injury, is fairly\ntraceable, that's the standing -- the standard\nhere, fairly traceable to the host, if you\nwill, authorizing statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cooper",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the injury is fairly\ntraceable to the statute that gave birth,\nMr. Chief Justice, as you say, to the\nregulation itself. It -- it did, indeed, visit\nthe immediate injury on us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-12",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "cf97b7bcda1b4ed93e28183909ee53b696d429648fe4ada8ba48f85ec7629fa9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-cf97b7bcda1b-0004-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
